  "verbalization": "(+)-Actinidine is implicated in the interaction with Jurkat through a series of molecular pathways that converge on the cell surface receptor Asialoglycoprotein receptor 2 (ASGPR2) and the enzyme Endothelial lipase. The evidence suggests that (+)-Actinidine acts as a target for both ASGPR2 and Endothelial lipase, with these targets ultimately leading to a relationship with Jurkat. The high scores in the paths indicate a strong, consistent link between (+)-Actinidine and Jurkat, suggesting a potential mechanism involving the modulation of lipid metabolism or receptor signaling pathways. The presence of multiple distinct targets—ASGPR2 and Endothelial lipase—indicates that (+)-Actinidine may exert its effects through different mechanisms, possibly by influencing distinct cellular processes. The integration of these pathways highlights the complexity of the relationship, with Jurkat potentially being a downstream effector of these molecular interactions.",
